eval("__webpack_require__.r(__webpack_exports__);\n/* harmony export */ __webpack_require__.d(__webpack_exports__, {\n/* harmony export */   blogPosts: () => (/* binding */ blogPosts)\n/* harmony export */ });\nconst blogPosts = [\n    {\n        id: 'future-digital-design-2026',\n        title: 'The Future of Digital Design in 2026',\n        excerpt: 'Explore the upcoming trends in UI/UX design, from AI-driven interfaces to immersive 3D experiences.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>The Rise of AI-Driven Interfaces</h2>\n      <p>As we move further into 2026, Artificial Intelligence is no longer just a buzzword; it's a fundamental component of the design process. AI-driven interfaces are adapting to user behaviors in real-time, providing highly personalized experiences that were previously impossible.</p>\n      \n      <h2>Immersive 3D Experiences</h2>\n      <p>With hardware becoming more powerful and accessible, web and mobile applications are increasingly incorporating 3D elements. These aren't just for show—they enhance usability and make digital environments feel more tangible.</p>\n      \n      <h2>Focus on Accessibility</h2>\n      <p>Design in 2026 is inherently inclusive. There's a stronger emphasis than ever on ensuring that digital products are accessible to everyone, regardless of their abilities. This means better contrast, clear typography, and thoughtful navigation structures.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Apr 15, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_design.png',\n        author: 'Jane Doe',\n        category: 'Design Trends'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'maximizing-roi-social-media',\n        title: 'Maximizing ROI with Social Media Marketing',\n        excerpt: 'Learn strategies to boost engagement and conversion rates across different social media platforms.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Understanding Your Audience</h2>\n      <p>The foundation of any successful social media campaign is a deep understanding of your target audience. You need to know where they spend their time, what kind of content they engage with, and what problems they are trying to solve.</p>\n      \n      <h2>Data-Driven Decisions</h2>\n      <p>Relying on gut feelings is a thing of the past. Today's marketers use advanced analytics tools to track performance and adjust their strategies on the fly. Metrics like engagement rate, click-through rate, and conversion rate are critical.</p>\n      \n      <h2>The Power of Video Content</h2>\n      <p>Short-form video continues to dominate social media. Platforms like TikTok, Instagram Reels, and YouTube Shorts are essential channels for reaching younger demographics. The key is creating authentic, engaging videos that capture attention quickly.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Apr 10, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_marketing.png',\n        author: 'John Smith',\n        category: 'Digital Marketing'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'brand-identity-matters',\n        title: 'Why Brand Identity Matters More Than Ever',\n        excerpt: 'A strong brand identity is crucial in a saturated market. Discover how to build a brand that resonates.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Consistency is Key</h2>\n      <p>A strong brand identity is built on consistency. From your logo and color palette to your tone of voice and customer service, every interaction a person has with your brand should feel cohesive.</p>\n      \n      <h2>Building Trust</h2>\n      <p>Consumers are increasingly skeptical of brands. A clear, authentic identity helps build trust. When people know what you stand for and what they can expect from you, they are more likely to become loyal customers.</p>\n      \n      <h2>Standing Out</h2>\n      <p>In a saturated market, you need to find a way to stand out. A unique brand identity sets you apart from your competitors. It's not just about looking different; it's about being different in a way that resonates with your audience.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Apr 05, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_tech.png',\n        author: 'Alice Johnson',\n        category: 'Branding'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'mastering-typography-web',\n        title: 'Mastering Typography for the Web',\n        excerpt: 'Typography is more than just picking a nice font. It is the core of web accessibility and readability.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Hierarchy and Readability</h2>\n      <p>Using the correct hierarchy with H1, H2, and H3 tags ensures your readers can scan the content. A well-chosen font pairing makes it a pleasant reading experience.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Mar 28, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_design.png',\n        author: 'Emily White',\n        category: 'Web Design'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'seo-best-practices-2026',\n        title: 'SEO Best Practices for 2026',\n        excerpt: 'Search engine algorithms are constantly evolving. Here is what you need to know to stay on top of the SERPs.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>User Intent is Everything</h2>\n      <p>Focusing on exact match keywords is no longer enough. You must understand what the user is actually looking for and answer their question better than anyone else.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Mar 20, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_tech.png',\n        author: 'Michael Brown',\n        category: 'SEO'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'color-psychology-marketing',\n        title: 'Color Psychology in Marketing',\n        excerpt: 'How the colors you choose impact consumer behavior and brand perception.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>The Emotion of Color</h2>\n      <p>Red can evoke urgency and passion, while blue creates a sense of trust and security. Understanding these associations is critical for effective marketing.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Mar 12, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_marketing.png',\n        author: 'Sarah Davis',\n        category: 'Digital Marketing'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'building-scalable-react-apps',\n        title: 'Building Scalable React Applications',\n        excerpt: 'Best practices for structuring your React codebase as your project grows.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Component Architecture</h2>\n      <p>Breaking down UI into small, reusable components is key. Using context or state management libraries like Redux helps manage complex states globally.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Mar 05, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_tech.png',\n        author: 'David Wilson',\n        category: 'Development'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'power-of-minimalism',\n        title: 'The Power of Minimalism in UI Design',\n        excerpt: 'Less is often more. How minimalist interfaces improve usability and focus.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Whitespace is Your Friend</h2>\n      <p>Giving elements room to breathe reduces cognitive load. Focus only on the essential features that provide value to the user.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Feb 25, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_design.png',\n        author: 'Chris Taylor',\n        category: 'UI/UX Design'\n    },\n    {\n        id: 'future-of-ecommerce',\n        title: 'The Future of E-Commerce Experiences',\n        excerpt: 'How AR and personalized shopping are transforming online retail.',\n        content: `\n      <h2>Virtual Try-Ons</h2>\n      <p>Augmented Reality is allowing customers to visualize products in their own space before buying, dramatically reducing return rates.</p>\n    `,\n        date: 'Feb 15, 2026',\n        img: '/images/blog_marketing.png',\n        author: 'Jessica Lee',\n        category: 'E-Commerce'\n    }\n];\n//# sourceURL=[module]\n//# sourceMappingURL=data:application/json;charset=utf-8;base64,\n//# sourceURL=webpack-internal:///(ssr)/./src/data/blogPosts.js\n");

